id: pm-g2zzus
title: "A repeatable boolean extension switch mixed in attached and bare forms (--many=false --many) loses its bare occurrences, because Commander never sees the attached form"
description: "Found 2026-11-14 while fixing pm-gh1726 on the built CLI. A flag declared value_type boolean with repeatable: true is a switch (value_arity none), so Commander registers it without a value placeholder: a bare --many reaches the list accumulator, while --many=false is unknown to Commander and is read only by the loose parser from command.args. coerceAccumulatedLooseOption in src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts orders values from the loose occurrences whenever any exist, so the Commander-held bare values are dropped: pm <cmd> --many=false --many delivers [false] instead of [false, true], and --many --many=false delivers [false] instead of [true, false]. All-bare (--many --many, fixed in the same PR to [true, true]) and all-attached forms are unaffected. Fix direction: derive list-switch occurrences in argv order from the captured COMMAND_OPTION_TOKENS with the existing scanArgvScope grammar (refuseConflictingArgvOptionSpellings already resolves each spelling with Commander semantics), instead of mixing Commander's accumulator with the loose occurrence list. Duplicate check: searched repeatable boolean switch attached value order argv; pm-wlxf8f (closed) owns scalar spelling conflicts, pm-853a (closed) value-arity predicates; nothing owns list-switch occurrence order."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: argv,cli,extensions,flags
created_at: "2026-11-14T16:53:28.191Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-23T10:55:36.638Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-23T09:40:01.315Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-23T09:40:01.315Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "pm <cmd> --many=false --many delivers [false, true] and --many --many=false delivers [true, false] on the built CLI; Occurrence order for list switches comes from the same argv scanner that resolves spelling conflicts, so a token consumed as another option's value is never counted; An in-process spec drives mixed, bare-only and attached-only forms, with a negative control showing the pre-fix loss"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "orderArgvRepeatableSwitchOccurrences (src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts) re-derives repeatable switch occurrences from the captured option tokens with the scanArgvScope walk the spelling-conflict check uses (resolveArgvSpelling gained a tracks selector; the sink reports attached values), and extractCommandScopedOptions passes the reordered source to the shared coercer. collectCommandOptionScopes is shared by both callers."
expected_result: "pm <cmd> --many=false --many delivers [false, true] and --many --many=false delivers [true, false]; a token another option consumed is never counted"
actual_result: "Built-CLI cases pass for both mixes, a three-occurrence mix, attached-only and a consumed token (--many --from-tracker --many=false is [true]); unit spec covers short alias, ancestor scope, --no-many and the unchanged-source paths; negative control fails as recorded"
